          %h4#almost_partitions Almost partitions
          %p
            Recall that a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition"} partition
            of a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+subsets"} family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒫
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
            of subsets of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (the
            %em parts
            of the partition) such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            of the parts and any two distinct parts are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+sets"} disjoint
            (or better, for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+subset"} inhabited
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a probability space, we may relax both conditions: for the union of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+set"} full set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+sets"} null sets
            (or better, for constructive mathematics, that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = B
            when
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^*(A \cap B) \gt 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^*
            is the
            %span.newWikiWord
              outer measure
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/outer+measure"} ?
            corresponding to
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
            For definiteness, call such a collection of subsets a
            = succeed ";" do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                \-almost partition
            = succeed "-almost" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
