          %h2#References References
          %h3#ReferencesGeneral General
          %p
            The concept of entropy was introduced, by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Clausius"} Rudolf Clausius
            in 1865, in the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/information+theory"} information theory
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claude+Shannon"} Claude Shannon
            in 1948, to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+von+Neumann"} John von Neumann
            in 1955, to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodic+theory"} ergodic theory
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrey+Kolmogorov"} Andrey Kolmogorov
            and Sinai in 1958, and to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+dynamics"} topological dynamics
            by Adler, Konheim and McAndrew in 1965.
          %p A survey at the introductory level:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              \.
              %em What is Entropy?
              (2024). (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.09232"}> arXiv:2409.09232
              ).
          %p
            Survey with an eye towards
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+entropy"} black hole entropy
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ted+Jacobson"}> Ted Jacobson
              ,
              %em Entropy from Carnot to Bekenstein
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.07839"}> arXiv:1810.07839
              )
          %h3#ReferencesInQuantumProbabilityTheory In quantum probability theory
          %p
            Discussion of entropy in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+probability+theory"} quantum probability theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
            understood as positive linear functionals on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+observables"} of observables
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+algebra"} operator algebraic
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} states on star-algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrices"} density matrices
            defined via the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GNS+construction"} GNS construction
          %p Introduction and survey:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingemar+Bengtsson"}> Ingemar Bengtsson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+%C5%BByczkowski"} Karol Życzkowski
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometry of Quantum States — An Introduction to Quantum Entanglement
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511535048"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511535048
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrices"} density matrices
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entropy"} entropy
            in quantum probability, via the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GNS+construction"} GNS construction
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+P.+Balachandran"}> A. P. Balachandran
                , T. R. Govindarajan, Amilcar R. de Queiroz, A. F. Reyes-Lega, Section II of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic approach to entanglement and entropy
                %strong 88
                (2013) 022301 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.1300"}> arXiv:1301.1300
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.88.022301"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevA.88.022301
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+P.+Balachandran"}> A. P. Balachandran
                , A. R. de Queiroz, S. Vaidya,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Entropy of Quantum States: Ambiguities
                %strong 128
                (2013) 112 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1212.1239"}> arXiv:1212.1239
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1140/epjp/i2013-13112-3"} doi:10.1140/epjp/i2013-13112-3
            %li
              %p
                Paolo Facchi, Giovanni Gramegna, Arturo Konderak,
                %em Entropy of quantum states
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.12611"}> arXiv:2104.12611
                )
            %li
              %p
                Erling Størmer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Entropy in operator algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/AST_1995__232__211_0/"} web
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/article/AST_1995__232__211_0.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            In quantum mechanics, the basic notion is the von Neumann entropy defined in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrix"} density matrix
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebra"} von Neumann algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Irving+Segal"}> I. E. Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A note on the concept of entropy
          %p
            %a{:href => "#RelativeEntropy"} Relative entropy
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/states"} states
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebras"} von Neumann algebras
            was introduced in
          %ul
            %li#Araki
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Huzihiro+Araki"}> Huzihiro Araki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Relative entropy of states of von Neumann algebras
              %p
                11 (1976) 809–833 (
                %a{:href => "https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/2833"}> pdf
                )
          %p A note relating I. Segal’s notion to relative entropy is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Longo"}> Roberto Longo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em A note on continuous entropy
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03357"} arXiv:2202.03357
          %p A large collection of references on quantum entropy is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Fuchs"}> Christopher Fuchs
              ,
              %em References for research in quantum distinguishability and state disturbance
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.perimeterinstitute.ca/personal/cfuchs/BigRef.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h3#category_theoretic_and_cohomological_interpretations Category theoretic and cohomological interpretations
          %p
            A discussion of entropy with an eye towards the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+spaces"} measure spaces
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Gromov"}> Mikhail Gromov
                ,
                %em In a search for a structure, Part I: On entropy
                (2012) (
                %a{:href => "https://www.ihes.fr/~gromov/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/structre-serch-entropy-july5-2012.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                %em State categories, closed categories, and the existence
                [of]
                = succeed "," do
                  %em semi-continuous entropy functions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ima.umn.edu/preprints/State-Categories-Closed-Categories-and-Existence-Semi-Continuous-Entropy-Functions"} web
          %p Category-theoretic characterizations of entropy are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/johnbaez/show/Entropy+as+a+functor"} Entropy as a functor
            %li
              %p
                Cheuk Ting Li,
                %em A Characterization of Entropy as a Universal Monoidal Natural Transformation
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.05742"}> arXiv:2308.05742
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p A (co)homological viewpoint is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Pierre Baudot,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Bennequin"} Daniel Bennequin
              = succeed "," do
                %em The homological nature of entropy
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.3390/e17053253"} doi
          %p
            (for an update see also the abstract of a talk of Baudot
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://calendar.math.cas.cz/content/information-cohomology-and-topological-information-data-analysis"} here
          %h3#ReferencesAxiomaticCharacterization Axiomatic characterizations
          %p After the concept of entropy proved enormously useful in practice, many people have tried to find a more abstract foundation for the concept (and its variants) by characterizing it as the unique measure satisfying some list of plausible-sounding axioms.
          %p
            A characterization of
            %a{:href => "#RelativeEntropy"} relative entropy
            on finite-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebras"} C-star algebras
            is given in
          %ul
            %li#Petz92
              D. Petz,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Characterization of the relative entropy of states of matrix algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.renyi.hu/~petz/pdf/52.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A simple characterization of von Neumann entropy of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrices"} density matrices
            (mixed
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
          %ul
            %li
              Bernhard Baumgartner,
              %em Characterizing Entropy in Statistical Physics and in Quantum Information Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.5727"}> arXiv:1206.5727
              )
          %p Entropy-like quantities appear in the study of many PDEs, with entropy estimates. For an intro see
          %ul
            %li
              L. C. Evans,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A survey of entropy methods for partial differential equations
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/bull/2004-41-04/S0273-0979-04-01032-8/"} web
              = succeed ");" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~evans/ams.entropy.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "." do
                %em Entropy and partial differential equations
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~evans/entropy.and.PDE.pdf"} pdf
        .revisedby
